{
  "_comment": [
    "Groups raw terms into the readable families the profile and dashboard show.",
    "Generic on purpose: no site-specific terms. Matching is case-insensitive.",
    "",
    "sequencing_approaches: regexes over a request's Project Type (csv tier).",
    "  First match wins, so put specific patterns before general ones.",
    "methods: inferred `assay` terms -> a method family. Specific assay names",
    "  (a named behavioral test, a vendor's rig) never reach a chart; only the",
    "  family does. Sequencing assays are excluded here: the request records",
    "  cover sequencing with better provenance.",
    "  Families are tried in order, first match wins: keep specific before general",
    "  (Electron microscopy before Microscopy).",
    "stage_bands: regexes over inferred `stage` terms -> an ordered band. Time after\n  a treatment or injury is its own band, not a developmental stage.",
    "tool_classes: inferred `gene` terms -> a genetic-tool class. Genes not",
    "  listed are biology, not tooling, and stay out of the toolkit view.",
    "languages: file extensions -> analysis language.",
    "Unmatched terms are counted and listed in the profile's appendix, so a",
    "missing mapping is visible rather than silently dropped."
  ],
